      <!-- ===================================================
           SECTION ONE: HOW I CAN COME IN (3D Flip Cards)
           =================================================== -->
      <section class="hww-hero-section" aria-labelledby="hww-title">
        <div class="rooms-container">
          <div class="hww-intro">
            <span class="whimsical-eyebrow">I COME IN</span>
            <h1 id="hww-title" class="hww-main-title">
              Somewhere between the problem <span class="italic-serif">and the result.</span>
            </h1>
            <p class="hww-lead-copy">
              That usually means getting close to your product, understanding the people evaluating it, and turning what makes it worth choosing into content they can use.
            </p>
            <p class="hww-hint-text">
              I come in through a focused content project or a broader BOFU content system. Tap a card to see what each involves.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Two ways to work together: focused projects or a connected BOFU content system. -->
          <div class="flip-deck-grid">
            <!-- CARD 01: BOFU CONTENT PROJECTS -->
            <div class="flip-card-scene">
              <div class="flip-card-inner" id="card-inner-1">
                <article class="flip-card-face flip-card-front" aria-labelledby="c1-front-title">
                  <div class="flip-card-top">
                    <span class="mosaic-stat">01</span>
                    <span class="mosaic-tag">PROJECT-BASED</span>
                  </div>
                  <h2 id="c1-front-title" class="flip-front-title">
                    BOFU content<br />projects.
                  </h2>
                  <p class="flip-front-desc">
                    A focused piece of work when you know what you need—or need help figuring out what deserves to exist.
                  </p>
                  <button type="button" class="flip-action-btn" aria-controls="card-inner-1" aria-expanded="false">
                    SEE WHAT I MAKE <span class="circle-chevron" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 100 100" focusable="false" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><circle cx="50" cy="50" r="46" fill="none" stroke="#1F2224" stroke-width="3.2"/><path d="M43 30 L63 50 L43 70" fill="none" stroke="#1F2224" stroke-width="3.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span>
                  </button>
                </article>

                <article class="flip-card-face flip-card-back" aria-label="BOFU content project formats and scope">
                  <div class="flip-card-top">
                    <span class="mosaic-tag">BOFU CONTENT PROJECTS</span>
                    <button type="button" class="flip-return-btn" aria-label="Flip card back to front">← FLIP BACK</button>
                  </div>

                  <div class="flip-back-scroll">
                    <h3 class="flip-back-headline">
                      Sometimes, you don't need a whole system. You need the right asset, properly thought through.
                    </h3>
                    <p class="flip-back-body">
                      I take on individual assets or batches of related content. We agree on the buyer, the angle, the evidence and what the content needs to help them decide before I start writing.
                    </p>

                    <div class="production-deliverables">
                      <span class="process-flow-label">WHAT I CAN HELP CREATE</span>

                      <div class="deliverable-item">
                        <strong>Comparison pages</strong>
                        <p>Help buyers understand the meaningful differences between your product and the alternatives.</p>
                      </div>
                      <div class="deliverable-item">
                        <strong>Alternatives pages</strong>
                        <p>Give people evaluating other options a useful reason to consider yours.</p>
                      </div>
                      <div class="deliverable-item">
                        <strong>Product and use-case content</strong>
                        <p>Connect what the product does to the problems and workflows buyers recognise.</p>
                      </div>
                      <div class="deliverable-item">
                        <strong>Buyer's guides and case studies</strong>
                        <p>Give buyers evidence, context and a clearer way to think through a decision.</p>
                      </div>
                      <div class="deliverable-item">
                        <strong>Thought leadership</strong>
                        <p>Develop useful points of view grounded in product knowledge and market understanding.</p>
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="dist-synthesis">
                      <p><strong>One asset or a related batch.</strong><br />
                      For batches, I scope around the research and production the pieces can share—not simply the number of articles on a list.</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <div class="flip-back-footer">
                    <button type="button" class="flip-return-pill">← Flip back</button>
                  </div>
                </article>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- CARD 02: BOFU CONTENT SYSTEM -->
            <div class="flip-card-scene">
              <div class="flip-card-inner" id="card-inner-2">
                <article class="flip-card-face flip-card-front" aria-labelledby="c2-front-title">
                  <div class="flip-card-top">
                    <span class="mosaic-stat">02</span>
                    <span class="mosaic-tag">STRATEGIC ENGAGEMENT</span>
                  </div>
                  <h2 id="c2-front-title" class="flip-front-title">
                    BOFU content<br />system.
                  </h2>
                  <p class="flip-front-desc">
                    A connected programme for teams that need more than individual pieces: direction, product understanding, execution and a way to improve the work.
                  </p>
                  <button type="button" class="flip-action-btn" aria-controls="card-inner-2" aria-expanded="false">
                    EXPLORE THE SYSTEM <span class="circle-chevron" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 100 100" focusable="false" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><circle cx="50" cy="50" r="46" fill="none" stroke="#1F2224" stroke-width="3.2"/><path d="M43 30 L63 50 L43 70" fill="none" stroke="#1F2224" stroke-width="3.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span>
                  </button>
                </article>

                <article class="flip-card-face flip-card-back" aria-label="BOFU content system process">
                  <div class="flip-card-top">
                    <span class="mosaic-tag">BOFU CONTENT SYSTEM</span>
                    <button type="button" class="flip-return-btn" aria-label="Flip card back to front">← FLIP BACK</button>
                  </div>

                  <div class="flip-back-scroll">
                    <h3 class="flip-back-headline">
                      Not a pile of articles. A connected programme built around how buyers evaluate your product.
                    </h3>
                    <p class="flip-back-body">
                      We connect what you know about the product with what buyers need to understand before they choose. The work moves from research and direction into production, distribution and improvement.
                    </p>

                    <div class="process-flow">
                      <span class="process-flow-label">HOW THE SYSTEM TAKES SHAPE</span>
                      <div class="flow-step">
                        <strong>Understand the buyer and positioning</strong>
                        <p>Review the ICP, customer knowledge, product positioning and the evidence behind your claims. Refine what needs sharpening.</p>
                      </div>
                      <div class="flow-divider" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
                      <div class="flow-step">
                        <strong>Map the buying decision</strong>
                        <p>Research buyer problems, use cases, evaluation criteria, objections, alternatives and the searches that signal intent.</p>
                      </div>
                      <div class="flow-divider" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
                      <div class="flow-step">
                        <strong>Get inside the product</strong>
                        <p>Study workflows, documentation and real use cases. Talk to the people who know the product and find credible angles.</p>
                      </div>
                      <div class="flow-divider" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
                      <div class="flow-step">
                        <strong>Build the narrative</strong>
                        <p>Translate product strengths into useful buyer-facing stories, supported by evidence and the right context.</p>
                      </div>
                      <div class="flow-divider" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
                      <div class="flow-step">
                        <strong>Plan and execute</strong>
                        <p>Prioritise and create the comparison, alternatives, use-case, guide, case study and thought leadership content the work calls for.</p>
                      </div>
                      <div class="flow-divider" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
                      <div class="flow-step">
                        <strong>Distribute, measure and improve</strong>
                        <p>Publish across relevant channels, then review search visibility, qualified engagement, conversions and pipeline influence where tracking allows.</p>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <div class="flip-back-footer">
                    <button type="button" class="flip-return-pill">← Flip back</button>
                  </div>
                </article>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Section Intermission / Breathing Space -->
          <div class="hww-transition-space">
            <span class="transition-eyebrow">TWO WAYS IN. ONE SHARED STARTING POINT.</span>
            <p class="transition-whisper">
              Understand the product. Understand the people deciding whether to buy it.
            </p>
          </div>
