      <!-- WHO THIS WORK IS FOR: buyer and business situations grounded in the Vevnit ICP. -->
      <section class="hww-context-section" aria-labelledby="hww-context-title">
        <div class="rooms-container">
          <div class="section-intro">
            <span class="whimsical-eyebrow">WHO THIS WORK IS FOR</span>
            <h2 id="hww-context-title" class="section-heading-editorial">
              The work <span class="italic-serif">tends to start here.</span>
            </h2>
            <p class="hww-context-intro">
              Usually, the content problem isn't simply that nobody is writing. Something is getting lost between what the product does, what buyers need to know and what the business needs content to do.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="hww-context-grid">
            <article class="why-mosaic-card hww-context-card">
              <div class="why-card-header">
                <span class="why-number">01</span>
                <span class="why-label">CAPACITY</span>
              </div>
              <h3 class="why-headline">Your team has priorities. Not enough hours.</h3>
              <p class="why-body">
                There's a strategy, a calendar or a list of ideas—but not enough specialist time to research, write and get the right work out.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article class="why-mosaic-card hww-context-card">
              <div class="why-card-header">
                <span class="why-number">02</span>
                <span class="why-label">PRODUCT UNDERSTANDING</span>
              </div>
              <h3 class="why-headline">Your product is easier to use than explain.</h3>
              <p class="why-body">
                The features and workflows make sense internally, but the value gets lost between technical detail and what buyers actually care about.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article class="why-mosaic-card hww-context-card">
              <div class="why-card-header">
                <span class="why-number">03</span>
                <span class="why-label">BUYER DECISIONS</span>
              </div>
              <h3 class="why-headline">Buyers are comparing. Your content isn't helping them decide.</h3>
              <p class="why-body">
                You need useful comparisons, alternatives, use cases and buying guidance that answer the questions prospects have before talking to sales.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article class="why-mosaic-card hww-context-card">
              <div class="why-card-header">
                <span class="why-number">04</span>
                <span class="why-label">CONTENT PERFORMANCE</span>
              </div>
              <h3 class="why-headline">There's activity. You need a clearer commercial contribution.</h3>
              <p class="why-body">
                Traffic and publishing alone aren't enough. You want content tied to qualified engagement, product consideration, demos, trials or pipeline.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>

          <div class="hww-readiness-note">
            <div>
              <span class="why-label">A USEFUL STARTING POINT</span>
              <h3>We don't need a perfect brief. We do need something real to work with.</h3>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p>
                You don't need a finished ICP or perfectly polished positioning. Refining those can be part of the work. I do need a live product, an identifiable audience, some useful customer or product knowledge, access to the people who know the product and a meaningful objective for the content.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

